{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/877721-sidereals-wfhl-dodge-the-ewer","id":877721,"title":"[Sidereals:WFHL] Dodge : The Ewer","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Sidereal Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-04-29T08:30:47-07:00","id":877721,"title":"[Sidereals:WFHL] Dodge : The Ewer","content":"<b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">DODGE : THE EWER</span></span></b><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#434343\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">THE SCRIPTURE OF THE HUNTED MAIDEN</span></span></b><br /> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Once, there was a maiden\u2026</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>\u2026who was driven from her land.</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Great black stags chased her, and their eyes shone blue.</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Monsters scrambled after her through the bush, though they found her not.</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Stumbling on a log, she fell; and thought to surrender, and end the torment of the hunt; but then, she stood, and stuck out her tongue at the dark woods behind her.</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>\u201cLove is smiling at your troubles,\u201d she said.</i></span></span></div> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Ewer is the sign of partnerships based in affection, of romantic pursuit or for the love of some other dream. In its ascending aspects, it is the sign of enduring adoration, flirtation, seduction and coquettish banter. In its descending precincts, it is the sign of the devouring matriarch and of thoughtless, obsessive or impossible love. It is the sign of the marriage-seeker, the idealist, the revolutionary and the good monk. The Ewer is the sign of incestuous couplings and amphibians.</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#434343\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Trappings</span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Ewer bears flowers and a work of poetry. He is blissfully happy and in love with love. He wears his finest clothing to see his beloved.</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#434343\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Correlations</span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Love, motherhood, righteousness, idealism, monastic duty, obsession, seduction, dreams and fantasies, courtship and romantic chases</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:purple\"><b><i>Resplendent Destiny of the Ewer</i></b></span><br /> <b>Cost:</b> - (10m); <b>Mins:</b> Dodge 1, Essence 1<br /> <b>Type:</b> Permanent<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> None<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Permanent<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> None<br /> <br /> Create a persona.<br /> An Essence 2 repurchase more fully realizes the persona; the Sidereal increases her Appearance by 1, to a maximum of 6, as she always looks like her best self.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:purple\"><b><i>Absence</i></b></span><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 2m; <b>Mins:</b> Dodge 2, Essence 1<br /> <b>Type:</b> Reflexive<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> None<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> None<br /> <br /> Never more is the Ewer missed than when it is absent. The Sidereal draws on this truth, ignoring all penalties to her Evasion against an attack.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:purple\"><b><i>Ever Increasing Affection</i></b></span><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 1m; <b>Mins:</b> Dodge 2, Essence 1<br /> <b>Type:</b> Reflexive<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Perilous, Stackable<br /> <b>Duration:</b> One Scene<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> None<br /> <br /> Every chase is a romance, and every romance, a chase. With soft and sly steps, the Sidereal can drive her hunters mad with the need to bring an end. Ever Increasing Affection may be used to enhance her Evasion; an opponent who attacks her and misses must pay 1 initiative in order to take any actions other than pursuing or attacking her again; this ends when he manages to successfully strike the Sidereal, if she releases the charm, if she is crashed, if she leaves the combat, or when the scene ends. She may use Ever Increasing Affection multiple times against the same opponent, stacking it up to (Essence) times, and may distract any number of enemies. Ever Increasing Affection may not be used against battle groups.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:purple\"><b><i>Frenzied Lover's Flight</i></b></span><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 3m; <b>Mins:</b> Dodge 3, Essence 1<br /> <b>Type:</b> Supplemental<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> None<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> None<br /> <br /> An arrow in flight is less swift than a lover racing to their beloved. The Sidereal's stride lengthens to match, her pace quickens as she closes upon her goal. Frenzied Lover's Flight supplements a Rush; she re-rolls 10s until 10s fail to appear, accumulating the successes. If she in the Destiny of the Ewer, she also adds the difference between her Appearance and her target's Resolve as non-charm bonus dice.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:purple\"><b><i>Chasing Impossible Dreams</i></b></span><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 3m; <b>Mins:</b> Dodge 3, Essence 1<br /> <b>Type:</b> Supplemental<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> None<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Absence or Ever Increasing Fondness<br /> <br /> For all that he promises, the Ewer deals more in dreams than substance. The Sidereal drinks deep and becomes like a dream. something to be chased but never caught. Chasing Impossible Dreams enhances her attempts to disengage; increase the target number of opponent's rolls opposing her disengagement by 1. If she is in the Destiny of the Ewer, they also re-roll 10s until 10s fail to appear, discarding successes from these rolls.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:purple\"><b><i>Love is Blinding</i></b></span><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 2m; <b>Mins:</b> Dodge 3, Essence 1<br /> <b>Type:</b> Reflexive<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Perilous<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Ever Increasing Fondness or Trouble Reduction Strategy<br /> <br /> A provocative wink can drive even the best to distraction, blinding them to other dangers. The Sidereal may use Love Is Blinding when anyone she has enchanted with Ever Increasing Affection takes an action against someone other than her. The attacker briefly loses his ability to clearly see anything other than her; his actions which depend on visual acuity suffer a penalty equal to the initiative he forfeits for taking the action.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:purple\"><b><i>Scent of Rose and Orchid</i></b></span><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 5m; <b>Mins:</b> Dodge 2, Essence 2<br /> <b>Type:</b> Simple<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Mute<br /> <b>Duration:</b> One Scene<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> None<br /> <br /> Sometimes those in love attempt to deny their own hearts, but the Ewer always sees through the lies we tell ourselves. The Sidereal automatically knows if anyone out to Medium range is in love, although not who, with whom, or the nature of their affection. If she uses a Read Intentions roll to divine any of this information from someone, she gains (Essence) non-charm successes, and can contest magic that would normally conceal her subject's true feelings.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:purple\"><b><i>Trouble Reduction Strategy</i></b></span><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 1wp; <b>Mins:</b> Dodge 3, Essence 2<br /> <b>Type:</b> Reflexive<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Perilous<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> None<br /> <br /> Love is not true unless it is shared, and the best drink requires companions to assist. The Sidereal may use any reflexive, instant Dodge charm on behalf of an ally she can see within Long range. Her beneficiary may refuse the effect at no cost to themselves, although any costs the Sidereal has paid remain spent.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:purple\"><b><i>Laughing at Danger</i></b></span><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 2m; <b>Mins:</b> Dodge 3, Essence 2<br /> <b>Type:</b> Reflexive<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Perilous<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Trouble Reduction Strategy or Frenzied Lover's Flight<br /> <br /> Those who drink deep of the Ewer gain the courage to laugh in the face of danger, and sometimes laughter is all that is needed. The Sidereal gains 1 initiative from a successful application of her Evasion against an attack made at close range.<br /> At Essence 3, she may pay 6m and increase the duration of Laughing at Danger to One scene. An Essence 5 repurchase allows her to draw initiative from attacks made against her at any range.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:purple\"><b><i>Snappy Banter Approach</i></b></span><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 3m; <b>Mins:</b> Dodge 3, Essence 2<br /> <b>Type:</b> Reflexive<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Mute<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Frenzied Lover's Flight or Scent of Rose and Orchid<br /> <br /> As many a drunk may attest, the Ewer always gets the last word. In response to any inspire or instill action she witnesses, the Sidereal may make one of her own against the speaker. If she does, decrease his Resolve by the number of 1s and 2s he rolled on his action. If this reduces his Resolve to 0, he is unable to spend Willpower to resist the Sidereal's influence.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:purple\"><b><i>Avoidance Kata</i></b></span><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 2m; <b>Mins:</b> Dodge 4, Essence 2<br /> <b>Type:</b> Simple<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Psyche<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Chasing Impossible Dreams or Love Is Blinding<br /> <br /> Everyone has, at one point or another, gone to drink deep only to find that the Ewer was empty. The Sidereal joins their misapprehension, avoiding a potentially unpleasant confrontation. She rolls (Dexterity + Dodge) against a difficulty of (3 + the number of actions she has taken); if successful, she vanishes, reappearing somewhere else she could plausibly have been instead. Anyone who witnesses her vanish must spend (higher of Essence or 3) Willpower to remember that she was present. She may only attempt to use Avoidance Kata once a scene.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:purple\"><b><i>Sweet Flirtation Smile</i></b></span><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 1wp; <b>Mins:</b> Dodge 5, Essence 2<br /> <b>Type:</b> Reflexive<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Perilous<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Love is Blinding or Laughing at Danger<br /> <br /> There may be nothing in Creation more dangerous than a pretty smiling man; certainly, they have been the downfall of more princes and empires than any number of armies and assassins, while their jealousies and lusts have brought ruin to countless great and small. The Sidereal may use Sweet Flirtation Smile when anyone she has enchanted with Ever Increasing Affection attacks another to gain the initiative they lose.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:purple\"><b><i>Armored in Ideals</i></b></span><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 7m; <b>Mins:</b> Dodge 4, Essence 3<br /> <b>Type:</b> Simple<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Perilous<br /> <b>Duration:</b> One Scene<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Laughing at Danger or Snappy Banter Approach<br /> <br /> The Ewer is a source of courage; many a woman has found a drink to give them the spine to act against what they know is wrong. The Sidereal may use Armored in Ideals when unarmored and acting to defend or further a Principle; doing so briefly increases her soak and hardness. A minor intimacy adds 5 soak and 4 hardness; a major intimacy adds 8 soak and 7 hardness; a defining intimacy adds 11 soak and 10 hardness. Withering attacks have their minimum damage reduced by 1, 2 or 3 when striking her.<br /> If the Sidereal is hit and dealt damage, either withering or decisive, Armored In Ideals ends and the principle she drew upon goes numb and cannot be used again for any purpose until a weak has passed. The soak and hardness from Armored in Ideals is never compatible with other sources of soak or hardness.<br /> An Essence 4 repurchase allows her to increase Armored in Ideals' duration to Indefinite. When active, her horoscope proclaims her eternal championship of the driving principle. If any effect reduces the driving principle in strength, it immediately ends the effect of Armored in Ideals.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:purple\"><b><i>Smiling At Your Troubles</i></b></span><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 5m, 1wp; <b>Mins:</b> Dodge 5, Essence 3<br /> <b>Type:</b> Reflexive<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Perilous<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Avoidance Kata or Sweet Flirtation Smile<br /> <br /> Woman is born to trouble and strife, and there can be no escape. All she can do, ultimately, is learn to smile at her troubles and let them pass aside. Once per scene, the Sidereal dodges any attack from any source without contest, even uncountable recurring damage. Smiling At Your Troubles may be reset by evading a decisive attack from a significant opponent which results in that opponent crashing.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:purple\"><b><i>Sick with Need</i></b></span><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 6m, 1wp; <b>Mins:</b> Dodge 4, Essence 4<br /> <b>Type:</b> Simple<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> None<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Sweet Flirtation Smile or Armored In Ideals<br /> <br /> Of all the diseases to afflict humanity, there may be none worse than the ache that comes from loving without being loved in return. The Sidereal learns to inflict this love sickness upon her target, filling them with a wasting need. This requires touching her victim; in combat, this is a difficulty 2 gambit. If successful, the victim is afflicted with love sicknesses. Treat this as an illness with a morbidity of the object of the obsession's Appearance and an interval of one week, save that it is resisted with (Wits + Integrity) rather than (Stamina + Resistance). In any scene in which the object of the obsession reciprocates the afflicted's love, the afflicted does not suffer from the symptoms of the disease. Mortals who reach the final phase of the illness will either waste away from want, or undertake a suicidally foolish action to prove their love.<br /> At Essence 5, the Sidereal may instead afflict her target with love towards a principle the Sidereal holds. In this case, the interval rises to one month, the Morbidity equals (strength of intimacy + Essence), and the victim is relieved of his symptoms in any scene in which he undertakes at least a Minor labor in the service of their principle.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:purple\"><b><i>Neighborhood Relocation Strategy</i></b></span><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 10m, 1wp; <b>Mins:</b> Dodge 5, Essence 4<br /> <b>Type:</b> Simple<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Prayer Strip<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Indefinite<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Smiling At Your Troubles or Sick With Need<br /> <br /> It is the duty of the Chosen to keep Creation safe; not only themselves, not only their friends and family, but everyone across the face of the world. When vast disaster threaten, it becomes incumbent upon them to change the face of the world in the service to that duty. The Sidereal places posts around a city, town or other contiguous area, each one bearing a prayer strip marked with the Scripture of the Hunted Maiden, and then activates Neighborhood Relocation Scheme. A bright blue fence springs up between the posts, and a dozen dozen azure tethers bind themselves between the Sidereal and the prayer strips. The marked area comes with the Sidereal as she moves- natural landmarks shifting to accommodate as best they can. For each day after the first that the Sidereal continues to rearrange Creation with Neighborhood Relocation Strategy, she rolls a number of dice equal to the days she has already used in this year, gaining Paradox equal to the number of successes rolled. If she suffers a backlash or is incapacitated, the effect ends immediately.<br /> Neighborhood Relocation Strategy cannot be used to break apart a single conceptual location; she cannot take one hour or one street from a town, or only part of a river. Nor can it be used to destroy or render the move area more uninhabitable than it previously was; a Manse-tomb hidden in a jungle would become a mist-shroud island if pulled to the center of the sea, for instance, or a city may become a vast city-ship or fleet of ships.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":169,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","user":"wastevens","date":". 04-29-2016, 01:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-29T08:54:19-07:00","id":877745,"title":"","content":"So I know that there is a tradition of interpreting the application of Ability Charms rather loosely for Sidereals (<i>Neighborhood Relocation Strategy</i> is a good example of how Dodge can be stretched pretty far). And I'm cool with that. But I can't see how <i>Scent of Rose and Orchid, Snappy Banter Approach</i>, or <i>Sick With Need</i> have anything to do with Dodge at all. The fluff connecting them to the Ewer makes sense, but I don't know that this is enough. There ought to be some connection to the underlying Ability. <i>Armored in Ideals</i> is less egregious since it is at least offering up a defensive benefit of some kind, but it doesn't seem to belong in Dodge either.<br /> <br /> Not trying to be a downer, I like a lot of the rest of this stuff. But those seem pretty out-of-place, even in the famously esoteric Sidereal tool kit. This might not be the case if, say, the whole Dodge tree revolved around leveraging Intimacies or something and so a Charm like <i>Scent </i>or <i>Snappy Banter </i>was indirectly supporting an Evasion strategy. But it doesn't, so they just stand out as weird for weird's sake.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Share your wonders in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop#post823884\" target=\"_blank\">The Artifact and Evocation Workshop</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1315-ferryman","name":"Ferryman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1315_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"960"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-29T09:10:02-07:00","id":877768,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ferryman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/877721-sidereals-wfhl-dodge-the-ewer?p=877745#post877745\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I know that there is a tradition of interpreting the application of Ability Charms rather loosely for Sidereals (<i>Neighborhood Relocation Strategy</i> is a good example of how Dodge can be stretched pretty far). And I'm cool with that. But I can't see how <i>Scent of Rose and Orchid, Snappy Banter Approach</i>, or <i>Sick With Need</i> have anything to do with Dodge at all. The fluff connecting them to the Ewer makes sense, but I don't know that this is enough. There ought to be some connection to the underlying Ability. <i>Armored in Ideals</i> is less egregious since it is at least offering up a defensive benefit of some kind, but it doesn't seem to belong in Dodge either.<br /> <br /> Not trying to be a downer, I like a lot of the rest of this stuff. But those seem pretty out-of-place, even in the famously esoteric Sidereal tool kit. This might not be the case if, say, the whole Dodge tree revolved around leveraging Intimacies or something and so a Charm like <i>Scent </i>or <i>Snappy Banter </i>was indirectly supporting an Evasion strategy. But it doesn't, so they just stand out as weird for weird's sake.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Eh, it's not so much being weird for weird's sake, as it is part of my overall effort of placing a greater emphasis on the constellation's themes for the charms rather than the ability- it's a part of folding the Resplendency effects and ideas into the charm trees while collapsing and eliminating the Colleges.<br /> <br /> (That's also why basically all the charms in Dodge have prereqs of X or Y - if all you want to a fairly normal defensive suite, you can get that without getting any of the emotion / social influence stuff.)<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-29T10:11:42-07:00","id":877845,"title":"","content":"I guess I'm of the school of thought that considers it less charming and more annoying when a player looks at his/her Charmset and goes &quot;Ooh, my Presence character would love to have <i>Snappy Banter Appr</i>- wait, what is a Presence Charm doing in Dodge? I don't even <i>have </i>Dodge. Why do I need to buy Dodge to get better at Presence? How does <i>that </i>work?&quot; I recognize this may be a matter of taste.<br /> <br /> Speaking of <i>Snappy Banter Approach</i>, it lists itself as a prerequisite.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Share your wonders in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop#post823884\" target=\"_blank\">The Artifact and Evocation Workshop</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1315-ferryman","name":"Ferryman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1315_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"960"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-29T10:24:24-07:00","id":877857,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ferryman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/877721-sidereals-wfhl-dodge-the-ewer?p=877845#post877845\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess I'm of the school of thought that considers it less charming and more annoying when a player looks at his/her Charmset and goes &quot;Ooh, my Presence character would love to have <i>Snappy Banter Appr</i>- wait, what is a Presence Charm doing in Dodge? I don't even <i>have </i>Dodge. Why do I need to buy Dodge to get better at Presence? How does <i>that </i>work?&quot; I recognize this may be a matter of taste.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I'm one of the weirdos that liked the weird charms philosophy of 1e Sidereals, and wanted to really run with it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ferryman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/877721-sidereals-wfhl-dodge-the-ewer?p=877845#post877845\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Speaking of <i>Snappy Banter Approach</i>, it lists itself as a prerequisite.</div> </div> </div> </div>&gt;.&gt;<br /> <br /> Avoidance Kata!<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-29T10:29:13-07:00","id":877864,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wastevens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/877721-sidereals-wfhl-dodge-the-ewer?p=877857#post877857\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Indeed <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I'm one of the weirdos that liked the weird charms philosophy of 1e Sidereals, and wanted to really run with it.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I like the weird charm locations too, but that philosophy works much better when you have only a handful charms in each tree. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-29T10:48:36-07:00","id":877890,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/877721-sidereals-wfhl-dodge-the-ewer?p=877864#post877864\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I like the weird charm locations too, but that philosophy works much better when you have only a handful charms in each tree.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Which- right, that's why I'm trying to ensure you can generally work around them.<br /> <br /> I've been trying to take some pains that, in each Tree, you *can* get a completely normal, ability-focused set of Charms, up to the Prayer Strip. Sometimes those will be kind of weird, but they're always tied directly in to the normal use of the ability.<br /> <br /> If you want to make a 'I'm very good at dodging' Sidereal up to the prayer strip, you take Absence, Chasing Impossible Dreams, Avoidance Kata, and Smiling At Your Troubles, Neighborhood Relocation Scheme.<br /> <br /> Now, if you want to make 'I'm the very best at the human conception of Dodging that a Sidereal can achieve'- you're going to need to also dip into Performance (for Defense of Shining Joy), Socialize (for revised You and Yours Stance) - maybe a few other dips. It's harder for a Sidereal to embody the human conception of a skill, because they naturally embody the meaning of those skills as reflected in the stars and as understood by the Maidens of Destiny.<br /> <br /> Being straightforwardly awesome is what the Solars are best at, and what they are for. And I won't begrudge folks that want Sidereals to be more straight forward. But they ain't the fate ninjas I'm making <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-29T10:50:13-07:00","id":877891,"title":"","content":"(Sidenote - I appreciate the feedback, even if the feedback is 'Meh, not to my taste'. I was starting to wonder if this effort was not simply amusing only to me, but actively being avoided &gt;&lt;)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-29T10:53:13-07:00","id":877893,"title":"","content":"Reading this gave me the wonderful idea of Sidereals charms being separated from abilities and tied only to constellations. The ability prerequisite for different charms in the tree could be from different abilities and they could focus purely on the expression of the conceptual.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my RPG podcast: <a href=\"http://thestorytold.libsyn.com\" target=\"_blank\">The Story Told</a><br /> Follow my ongoing Exalted Campaign: <a href=\"https://thefallofjiara.obsidianportal.com/adventure-log\" target=\"_blank\">The Fall of Jiara</a><br /> Check out my Community Content: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Chazz%20Kellner\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse....hazz%20Kellner</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/702-elfspeaker","name":"ElfSpeaker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar702_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-29T10:56:54-07:00","id":877896,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wastevens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/877721-sidereals-wfhl-dodge-the-ewer?p=877891#post877891\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(Sidenote - I appreciate the feedback, even if the feedback is 'Meh, not to my taste'. I was starting to wonder if this effort was not simply amusing only to me, but actively being avoided &gt;&lt;)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Nah. I've just been busy with work.<br /> <br /> I like that Sidereals aren't straight forward. Dipping into other caste abilities is a cool idea! It shows how interconnected caste abilities concepts are. I would try not to force say your Battles to dip into Dodge for Presence stuff. In theory it's an interesting idea; but at the gaming table, where XP is a limited resource, you will get some grumbling from the players.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-29T10:57:39-07:00","id":877897,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElfSpeaker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/877721-sidereals-wfhl-dodge-the-ewer?p=877893#post877893\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Reading this gave me the wonderful idea of Sidereals charms being separated from abilities and tied only to constellations. The ability prerequisite for different charms in the tree could be from different abilities and they could focus purely on the expression of the conceptual.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll throw a note of caution here, cause I toyed with the idea of 'mixed ability trees' (as opposed to 'weird abilities in unexpected trees') at first- but that was a significant problem in the 1e Lunars charm set, and would be compounded by needing to bump 25 abilities to max- raising 8 attributes was bad enough!<br /> <br /> For all the 2e Lunars did badly, remember- it's charm set was a massive improvement over the 1e charm set.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-29T11:47:08-07:00","id":877943,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/877721-sidereals-wfhl-dodge-the-ewer?p=877896#post877896\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like that Sidereals aren't straight forward. Dipping into other caste abilities is a cool idea! It shows how interconnected caste abilities concepts are. I would try not to force say your Battles to dip into Dodge for Presence stuff. In theory it's an interesting idea; but at the gaming table, where XP is a limited resource, you will get some grumbling from the players.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is really the point I was trying to make. I don't object to the idea in theory, but if it goes past a certain point (subjectively determined, natch) then it can easily become an irritation at the gaming table, and that ought to be avoided. High-concept stuff is cool as long as it is also fun to actually use. That can prove a difficult tightrope to walk successfully.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Share your wonders in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop#post823884\" target=\"_blank\">The Artifact and Evocation Workshop</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1315-ferryman","name":"Ferryman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1315_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"960"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-29T12:15:03-07:00","id":877968,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ferryman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/877721-sidereals-wfhl-dodge-the-ewer?p=877943#post877943\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is really the point I was trying to make. I don't object to the idea in theory, but if it goes past a certain point (subjectively determined, natch) then it can easily become an irritation at the gaming table, and that ought to be avoided. High-concept stuff is cool as long as it is also fun to actually use. That can prove a difficult tightrope to walk successfully.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yep. But I figure it's better to try something wild and fail in an interesting fashion <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}